<title>USA: United top Feb Washington DC cargo carrier.</title>
<headline>United top Feb Washington DC cargo carrier.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Airlines handled more import and export cargo at Washington DC's Dulles International Airport than all other carriers during February 1997, said the Metropolitan Washington Airports Authority.</p>
<p>The top 10 cargo carriers at Dulles International and the tonnage each carrier moved in February compared to the same month last year were:</p>
<p>				  Feb 97	  Feb 96</p>
<p>1.  United Airlines	11,371	   8,194</p>
<p>2.  Federal Express	 5,347	   5,052</p>
<p>3.  Airborne Express	  838	     918</p>
<p>4.  Lufthansa		   778	   1,099</p>
<p>5.  Virgin Atlantic	   691	     000</p>
<p>6.  British Airways	   671	     671</p>
<p>7.  Air France		  643	     749</p>
<p>8.  All Nippon Airways	424	     263</p>
<p>9.  United Parcel Service   386	     363</p>
<p>10. American Airlines	 283	     587</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706; fax +5017</p>
</text>
